WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.640
In real projects, I never found scenarios where the data is clean

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:07.239
so everything is messed up, the text values are inconsistent

3
00:00:07.239 --> 00:00:10.159
the numbers are stored as string values

4
00:00:10.159 --> 00:00:12.920
there are weird things inside the dates

5
00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.880
missing values are everywhere

6
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.680
so that means the data quality is really bad

7
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.360
and if you go and analyze the data like this

8
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.639
your result gonna be for sure wrong

9
00:00:22.639 --> 00:00:25.360
even if you write the SQL query correctly

10
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:28.559
so as a data analyst, you cannot analyze immediately

11
00:00:28.559 --> 00:00:31.479
first, you must clean and prepare the data

12
00:00:31.479 --> 00:00:36.119
and of course, SQL gives us enough tools and functions in order to do that

13
00:00:36.119 --> 00:00:39.680
so we have the string, the number and the date functions

14
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.200
we have functions that can handle the missing values, the nulls

15
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.840
and as well, we have a case statement in order to build standards in our data

16
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:51.520
those tools and functions are very important to understand and to learn

17
00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.880
in order to clean up and transform your messy data

18
00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:57.959
into something that is ready for analysis

19
00:00:57.959 --> 00:01:00.759
so we're gonna start with the first chapter with the first group

20
00:01:00.759 --> 00:01:03.080
the string functions, so let's go

